& [StableControlSurface] is Codex App Server over local stdio
  + [wire] is bidirectional headerless JSON-RPC 2.0 as newline-delimited JSON
  + [handshake] is exactly one initialize request followed by initialized notification before other methods
  + [thread] is thread/start or thread/resume with thread/started and later thread events
  + [turn] is turn/start, optional turn/steer, turn/interrupt, and terminal turn/completed
  + [events] are authoritative item/started and item/completed plus turn lifecycle notifications
  + [read_only] is thread sandbox read-only and turn sandboxPolicy type readOnly with networkAccess false
  + [approval] is approvalPolicy never; any server-initiated approval request is an unexpected fault in the Phase 2 profile
  + [ephemerality] is thread/start ephemeral true so the proof worker is not a durable conversation
  = decision: use the app-server wire directly from safe Rust because no official Rust Codex SDK is documented

& [StableCantorToolSurface] is the existing local MCP server
  + [configuration] is manager-owned exact cantor-mcp executable and exact compiled environment path supplied as app-server configuration overrides
  + [tool] is one model-visible read-only query_sop operation
  + [event] is an mcpToolCall item with server, tool, arguments, status, result, and error
  + [translation] is exact tool arguments to ProtocolRequest and exact structured result to ProtocolResponse before ecosystem admission
  = decision: reuse the already proved MCP projection rather than create a second semantic adapter

& [ExperimentalSurface] is not required by Phase 2
  + [dynamicTools] on thread/start and item/tool/call client callbacks require experimentalApi
  + [benefit] is a direct client-executed Cantor callback without prior MCP configuration
  + [cost] is experimental compatibility and a second tool projection
  = decision: defer dynamicTools; compare only after stable MCP live proof identifies an unmet requirement

& [EventAcceptanceProfile] is fail-closed
  + [required] is one completed Cantor query_sop mcpToolCall and one completed final agentMessage
  + [forbidden] is commandExecution, fileChange, webSearch, dynamicToolCall, collabAgentToolCall, approval request, user-input request, turn steer, and multiple Cantor calls
  + [completion] is only turn/completed status completed after the required completed items
  + [candidate] is the final agent message decoded through an explicit JSON output schema
  + [fault] is unexpected event, wrong identity, malformed JSON, oversized line, timeout, premature EOF, process failure, non-success tool, missing proof, or extra action

& [LocalSchemaEvidence] is version-specific and ignored runtime evidence
  + [generator] is codex app-server generate-json-schema
  + [schema_root] is C:\Project\Cantor\.local\codex-app-server-schema
